title The mechanism sentence seated, and three rooms given the insight
prompt Seat the mechanism-sentence rule then restart the loop, yet first decide whether to silo any of these insights to active-designing prose essays or external-research or foundations. Permission granted to follow all recommendations; the model stays Opus 5.
think Answer the siloing question with the design-rooms test before writing anything: would this still be worth reading if the code it describes were deleted. Three yeses and three different rooms. The durable claim about prose belongs in foundations. The read of outside sources, named with attribution, belongs in external-research by the silo law. The harness pattern and the two ways a sameness meter misleads belongs in active-designing, written in our own vocabulary only.
think Write the rule as a wall rather than a habit, since git-signing already proved that a rule a renderer or a reader can quietly break is worth a hook. tools/hooks/commit-msg already carries two rules; the mechanism sentence is the third, and it guards meaning where the other two guard rendering.
think Calibrate the threshold against real commits rather than guessing it. A flat floor of three distinct mechanism words fails 22 of 40, including honest short bodies. A length ladder measured better: sixty words or more wants three, twenty-five to fifty-nine wants one, under twenty-five passes free. Twenty-one of forty read below that floor and every honestly-short body cleared it.
think Put the vocabulary in one place and prove it. The hook and the scan each carry the same MECH_WORDS line between markers, and mechanism_words_agree.sh reads both out and compares them, because a wall counting different words from its own meter is worse than either alone. That is the dated-path lesson applied on the lap rather than after it.
obs The existing commit_message_guard_witness caught a false refusal within a minute of the wall going up: the public seed's root commit is 61 words with one mechanism word, because it describes a repository rather than a change. A guard proving its worth against its own author on the lap it is written.
obs Chose a named exemption over weakening the meter. The seed root is recognised by its Grain OS subject, which no component-prefixed commit in this tree can wear, and the wall scan proves both that the seed passes and that a borrower with the same body and a caravan subject is refused. Widening the vocabulary or raising the threshold would have bought the same pass by making the meter worse everywhere.
obs The honest limit is written into the rule, the foundation, and the witness header alike: the meter counts vocabulary, so it proves a floor rather than a comprehension. The note_path commit scores three and still left its reader unable to name the change. Word presence is the check; a reader reconstructing the diff is the standard.
obs Named the cause structurally rather than blaming a model. Radiant rewards the landed line, the commit rule asks every body to be written in that voice, and the naming law made titles into small poems -- so a capable author aims where the rules point. Same shape the negation ratchet found a day earlier in law-shaped prose. Two findings, one lesson.
obs The regime measurement is the part worth carrying: three of the four factors in the reported review-spiral regime are absent here, and the fourth -- 117 KB of always-on rules across 37 files -- is slightly worse than the ~110 KB the report measured. That is the one dial nobody chose deliberately.
loom witness=mechanism_sentence_witness verdict=green window=40 thin=21 ceiling=21 vocabulary=17
